ugh its propane pipeline, risk management, and other activities. Spire Inc. was formerly known as The Laclede Group, Inc. and changed its name to Spire Inc. in April 2016. Spire Inc. was founded in 1857 and is based in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott Edward Doyle | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $654K ranks in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Spire Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $5.2B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 5% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $344M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 26% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.26455132772959666},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Utilities sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 9% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Has Spire (NYSE:SR) Raised Its Common Dividend for Another Year?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/dividend/has-spire-nysesr-raised-its-common-dividend-for-another-year","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795524840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Is Spire (NYSE:SR) Stretching Its Dividend-Growth Streak Further?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/utility/is-spire-nysesr-stretching-its-dividend-growth-streak-further","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795412940.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Can Spire (NYSE:SR) Move Past Its Regulatory Questions?","source":"kalki